{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Big Argument"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Working it Out"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals For Possibility, Certainty, Suggestions and Expectations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">might </span> and <span class=\"strong\">could </span> to express <span class=\"underline\">possibility in the past and in the future </span>.  <span class=\"strong\">Can</span> is only used to talk about <span class=\"underline\">possibility in the present and future.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I'm sure you <span class=\"strong\">can make</span> it sound spontaneous.<br/>I <span class=\"strong\">can't say</span> I've noticed a big change so far. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> to express <span class=\"underline\">certainty</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">There <span class=\"strong\">must</span>  be something you can do about this phobia of yours.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">should</span>  , <span class=\"strong\">could</span>  , <span class=\"strong\">might</span>   and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>  to express <span class=\"underline\">suggestions</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span>call her for me.<br/>You <span class=\"strong\">might</span> want to rehearse for this.<br/>I <span class=\"strong\">could</span> write you a script!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to express<span class=\"underline\"> expectation</span>, you can use <span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">How am I  <span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> do that?</span>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions To Encourage Agreement"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Negative questions have a different meaning than regular questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use negative questions to confirm information you already know. It is another way to keep the conversation going. It is also a more indirect way of letting the other person know that you already know the answer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for some phrases that begin a negative question:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Don't you think ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Don't you think that might work? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Don't you want ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Don't you want her to know that you've been thinking about her?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Isn't it true ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Isn't it true that you've been thinking about her for ages?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wouldn't you like ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Wouldn't you like to know what she thinks about you?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Aren't you ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Aren't you curious about what she thinks of you?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to chicken out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to back out of something at the last minute"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I start dialing the number, but I chicken out before she can answer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about a difficult situation."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "paralyzed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to do anything out of fear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm paralyzed when it comes to speaking to girls on the phone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "phobia"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "intense fear of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There must be something you can do about your phobia of speaking on the phone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mention"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to refer to something without going into detail"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You could call Camilla and mention the fact that I'd like to go out with her."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spontaneous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "natural and genuine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I call Camilla, I won't sound spontaneous."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delivery"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the vocal and bodily behavior during a speech"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Delivery is very important when you read something."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "script"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a written speech, text or play"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you don't know what to say, I could write you a script."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm ideas on things to do on a first date."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph giving advice to David, who is going on his first date with a girl he met online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What should he do  and what is  is supposed to do?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include ideas on activities he could do in your community."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange with a partner and peer edit."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Add some more ideas about things to do."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about feelings and sensations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express possibility and certainty."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "